      "content": "Originalists anchor their arguments in the \"ancestral\" meaning found in the 1789 text, contending that a \"militia\" clause implicitly limited the right from operating on an individual basis. They rely heavily on historical analysis, particularly citing the Founding Fathers' views during the Bill of Rights debate to establish that the right to bear arms was a fundamental aspect of citizen participation in a militia structure, rather than a personal privilege. This approach often interprets the operative clause as inapplicable to charter schools, grazing groups, or those lacking a demonstrated militia registry, rejecting modern expansions of individual usage as contrary to the document's original structural intent.",
